{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably","id":544317,"title":"[Beast] Heroes: Necessarily Huge Dicks, or Just Probably?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-07T15:12:33-07:00","id":544317,"title":"[Beast] Heroes: Necessarily Huge Dicks, or Just Probably?","content":"A fair amount of people in the main Beast thread have requested that discussion of Hero generation and personality be moved elsewhere, as it threatens to become toxic. Well, this is kind of elsewhere, so let's go. Are Heroes necessarily gentlefolk of a highly disagreeable nature before their... Awakening? Exaltation? Hero-Homecoming?<br /> <br /> A question I'd personally like answered: Where does the bit about Slashers and Integrity 4 come from? I know Slashers says pre-Slashers need to be Morality 4 or lower to become magical serial killers, but I can't find a statement saying the Integrity threshold is the same. Given the difference between the Morality and Integrity systems I'd rather not make an assumption, so what's the story here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T15:55:11-07:00","id":544354,"title":"","content":"Inferring from the sample Heroes, those in the sample scenario, and the explicit description, there's already a degree of inadequacy or frustration with mundane life that seems to habitually characterize the kinds of people that become Heroes. However you or I may feel about that, I feel like that at least is very unambiguous from the text: You can see very clearly what the writers typify as a Hero and what they're like.<br /> <br /> Integrity is closer to a measure of mental stability than it is morality or lack of morality. I think that comes with the caveat that while it seems to measure a degree of mental and emotional welfare, having high Integrity doesn't necessarily mean you're a good or bad person. The three things that seem to cause Breaking Points are: Traumatic experiences, the supernatural, and violations of broad (but important) social moral codes and personal moral codes. So for a person who thinks stealing is the worst thing ever, it will totally be a breaking point for him, while it won't be for a person who cares nothing about that sort of thing. Both will probably experience breaking points if they encounter the supernatural, are tortured or do the torturing.<br /> <br /> The popular assessment seems to be that the low integrity is more likely to be from them being victims of trauma or the supernatural, lending itself to the troubling narrative that Heroes are in fact survivors rather than total jerks. I think it's more likely that the writers and developer were looking at imagining them as failing personal moral codes, like expectations of themselves, or being frustrated by perceived inadequacy and stuff like that, which would lead them to have the low Integrity that lends itself to their being Heroes.<br /> <br /> I would drop the line of thinking about Slashers, Morality and Integrity don't measure the same thing, and the number values mean something differently in the system.<br /> <br /> I'm not endorsing any of the above suggestions, I just think these are the things we can observe from the text. How you feel about it is up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:26:32-07:00","id":544467,"title":"","content":"From pgs 399 - 400 of the preview on the kickstarter; you can download the preview directly from the page if you would like to read it yourself. As this is a preview that is already open to the general public I don't see any problems with pasting from the text but if this is a no no just let me know and I'll erase it.<br /> <br /> &quot;In Chapters Two and Five, we mention that in order for a person to become a Hero, his Integrity rating can be no greater than four. For purposes of creating Hero characters, that\u2019s all you need to know, but it\u2019s important to unpack that idea so that you understand why that\u2019s the case and what it means for Heroes.<br /> <br /> Integrity, as explained in Chapter Four, is a game trait measuring the health of a person\u2019s soul and self-image. Integrity does not, by itself, measure whether a person is \u201cgood\u201d or not. It is not a measure of kindness or compassion. Certainly people with high Integrity traits tend to be strong of character, and strength of character leads to empathy and compassion, but it is possible to have a high Integrity rating and be harsh, cruel, or even violent. It simply means that the character is well aware of who and what he is.<br /> <br /> Incipient Heroes, though, lack that awareness. Their souls are weak, whether by nature or by difficult lives whittling away their Integrity. They tend to be shortsighted, self-centered (but not self-aware), and unfocused. A person can fall to this level of Integrity in any number of ways; when you are designing Heroes for your Beast chronicle, it\u2019s worthwhile to consider how it happened. You don\u2019t need to design breaking points for the character (though you can), nor do you need to detail how any given dot of Integrity was lost, but just a general sense of what happened to the character is enough. Did the character avoid talking to people out of belief that he was better? Did the character suffer some hardship and look for someone else to blame? Or is the answer more basic \u2014 is the character an abuser or a bully?<br /> <br /> As noted in Chapter Four, it\u2019s possible to lose Integrity from exposure to the supernatural, but this by itself doesn\u2019t usually reduce the trait low enough to qualify a person for becoming a Hero.Thematically, too, it\u2019s not appropriate for someone whose only \u201ccrime\u201d was bearing witness to the supernatural to become a Hero. Since Heroes are Storyteller-controlled character, you as Storyteller dictate why the Hero is the way he is, so make choices that allow the Hero to fulfill the appropriate role in the story. If the Hero is a sympathetic character, driven to hunt monstersby the relentless attacks of the supernatural, then you might be better served checking out Hunter: The Vigil (and perhaps using Beasts as antagonists). If, however, the Hero has deliberately shunned other people, defining himself by what he is not, what he hates, or the wrongs done to him, that\u2019s a perfect candidate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't feel that lends itself to the assessment of the Heroes being survivors and more to the what I suspect is the intended reading of the Heroes being people who were already prone to blaming and/or hating others for his or her failings as well as any life difficulties and in addition having already been in possession of a narcissistic world view before their encounter with a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","user":"Vedic","date":". 06-07-2015, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:53:24-07:00","id":544483,"title":"","content":"For some reason, reading it this time makes me think that the Integrity requirement is the weird bit. Considering Heroes are ST characters, I would have thought it utterly appropriate for authors to just make it a matter of fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:03:42-07:00","id":544485,"title":"","content":"It IS a matter of fiat, because the ST determines the Integrity of the NPCs. Using that Integrity as a guideline is one of the meeting points of mechanics and narrative. It tells you something about a Hero, and offers a mechanical conception of the difference between a person who can become/is a hero, and who cannot/is no longer a hero.<br /> <br /> The stats of any NPC are technically a matter of ST fiat, it's really about what the stat communicates either to player types who can somehow perceive Integrity in-character, or to the Storyteller who uses those mechanics to help foster a narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:24:06-07:00","id":544535,"title":"","content":"The game is very morally gray.<br /> <br /> Heroes might have been sympathetic at some point, but by the time they become heroes, they are no longer deserving of sympathy-Jason Voorhees was once a boy who was bullied ant camp due to his deformity and mental retardation and drowned because of it.<br /> <br /> Now he;''s a super zombie that kills people and has a body count in the hundreds.<br /> <br /> does he deserve sympathy?<br /> <br /> If the answer is no, then why does the guy who <i>might </i>have been bullied or abused but is just as if not more likely to have been the bully or abuser*or might just be a psychopath or extreme sociopath, or maybe is just a normal guy in a rut who blames everybody but himself for things that are his fault and tries to find someone to blame for things that are nobody's fault, who then had what is for all intents and purposes just a bad dream, and decided that if he kills the monster from his dream all of the world's problems will disappear and he'll be loved, never mind the monster in all likelihood ins't one of the ones that hurts people, and kills anyone who gets in their way, why does he deserve sympathy?<br /> <br /> Also, exposure to the supernatural causing Integrity 4 is explicitly called out in the text as being incredibly rare <i>and </i>not at all appropriate for the tone of the game for that to result in heroes. Continued abuse and/or bullying is likely to be in the same boat, especially as abusers an d bullies are both called out as potential heroes.<br /> <br /> Reading some people's complaints, I can't help but think that people are trying to turn a game about light gray-gray and dark gray-black morality into a game that's solid black and white. And then getting cuaght up on two details and using it to dress the heroes up in leather pants while branding all the Beasts with dark marks.<br /> <br /> Are there Beasts who are unrepentant Monsters that deserve to die? Yes. As there are with Vampires, werewolves, MAges, Hunters, Changelings, Prometheans, Sin-Eaters, Demons, Mummies, and Mortals.<br /> <br /> Are they the majority? Hell no. The book is very clear that Beasts, despite knowing and accepting that they are monsters, still have a human conscience and sometimes hate what they are, even f they don't want to go back to being human. There are numerous examples of Beastial feeding that causes no harm to anyone(in Particular the Tyrant Health Inspector is doing a great service in keeping filthy restaurants closed and reporting bribe attempts)<br /> <br /> Are there Heroes who are at low integrity from continued abuse or bullying? Probably.<br /> <br /> Are they the majority? Probably not.<br /> <br /> Are there Heroes who are right about the Beast who generated the nightmare that created them? Tes. But it's a broken clock scenario, to quote Matt. In General, the Beasts who are creating the Heroes are not the ones.who are hurting people frequently or even at all.<br /> <br /> Does occasionally being right justify the Hero's actions? No. No it does not. Because that's not why they're hunting the Beast, it's just a rationalization* The real reason they're hunting the Beast is because they blame all of their life's problems on the Beast, or because they think killing it will bring them glory. Or just because it's there. And besides, once you get to the point where you're willing to blow up a daycare with the kids inside because the caretaker is a Predator who hunts the spirits that feed off the children's nightmares during naptime, you're not a Hero, you're a lunatic.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">Rationalizations that would be valid points on their own are still rationalizations. Charles Bronson's character from <i>Death Wish</i> is still a serial killer even though he only kills criminals and is officially motivated by revenge for the rapes of his wife and daughter.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:28:17-07:00","id":544542,"title":"","content":"It also gives a guideline on how to 'rehabilitate' the Hero. When your little brother is convinced you are a man-eating abomination, do you really want to have to kill him? It is a little harder to deal with when you remember taking a bath with said Hero, or comforting them after a nightmare, or sharing Christmas dinner every year for 10 years.<br /> <br /> But it makes one hell of a good story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T17:44:57-07:00","id":544571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544542#post544542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also gives a guideline on how to 'rehabilitate' the Hero. When your little brother is convinced you are a man-eating abomination, do you really want to have to kill him? It is a little harder to deal with when you remember taking a bath with said Hero, or comforting them after a nightmare, or sharing Christmas dinner every year for 10 years.<br /> <br /> But it makes one hell of a good story.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a special case.<br /> <br /> I'm not a dev, but I'm pretty sure that special cases like that are why heroes can be rehabilitated in the first place..<br /> <br /> Of course, an Incarnate can cure a hero. an Incarnate who doesn't if they get the chance is kind of a dick, but that's another special case<br /> <br /> Also, how did the Beast's little brother become a hero? They need to hit Integ 4 to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T18:21:58-07:00","id":544632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasteful</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544483#post544483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, reading it this time makes me think that the Integrity requirement is the weird bit. Considering Heroes are ST characters, I would have thought it utterly appropriate for authors to just make it a matter of fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't in the leak, so it seems like it was added at the end, which might explain why it doesn't fit in with things like the example Heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T20:35:24-07:00","id":544735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544571#post544571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a special case.<br /> <br /> I'm not a dev, but I'm pretty sure that special cases like that are why heroes can be rehabilitated in the first place..<br /> <br /> Of course, an Incarnate can cure a hero. an Incarnate who doesn't if they get the chance is kind of a dick, but that's another special case<br /> <br /> Also, how did the Beast's little brother become a hero? They need to hit Integ 4 to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember the Incarnates getting special treatment when it comes rehabilitation. Will double check, thought it was just 'doesn't create or show up on radar'.<br /> <br /> Mind you I don't see why my example is all that special unless your doing a 'monster-of-the-week' thing. When <i>your Soul</i> makes a Hero, (as opposed to another Beast), it makes sense that you know the person. Familiar hunting ground and all that. Which in turn drives home the consequences of NOT feeding properly more clearly; you can see the effects. Maybe it's not your brother, maybe it's <i>your</i> co-worker, <i>your </i>best friend, <i>your </i> husband, <i>your </i> student, <i>your </i>dad or the bouncer at <i>your </i>regular drinking hole.<br /> Ok that last one is reaching but you get the idea.<br /> When it's someone else in your Brood who makes the Hero, then it is someone close to them and now you have to deal with it. Nothing comes from a vacuum; everything tries to fill one.<br /> <br /> And there is a lot of ways to get low Integrity, depending on the person. Walking in on your spouse cheating on you can be a breaking point, as can taking a drink after you've sworn you'll never go down that road again. Integrity 4 can mean a lot of different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:24:52-07:00","id":544762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544735#post544735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember the Incarnates getting special treatment when it comes rehabilitation. Will double check, thought it was just 'doesn't create or show up on radar'.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>No More Heroes:</b> The Beast\u2019s Soul does not cause Heroes to arise. Heroes might still seek the Beast out, but they cannot place Anathema on her and the Hero\u2019s gift of Heroic Tracking is of no use. <b>The Beast Incarnate can remove the Hero\u2019s abilities, granting him clarity and showing him exactly who he is in the scheme of things \u2014 an interloper, an intruder in a story that was never his.</b> With a simple touch, the Beast shows the Hero that no matter how unpleasant the occurrence that turned him into a Hero, no matter how terrifying the nightmare, it\u2019s not his place to end it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:27:34-07:00","id":544763,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn I read something about them being able to cure heroes.<br /> <br /> anyway, hero rules don't specify anything about the Beast's own soul picking out people they know to ravage(and it wou'dn't really make sense, since it's got the &quot;random rampage&quot; vibe which precludes picking a specific target.<br /> <br /> And it's a special case because most Beasts are not going to know their heroes.<br /> <br /> As for there being lots of ways to get lw integrity-yeah, not very many ways to hit integrity four.<br /> <br /> Not every braking point comes with integrity loss.<br /> <br /> Assuming the person is starting at 7(the average given integrity) it's going to take more than one breaking point to reach integrity four. I'll let someone more statistically minded calculate the exact details, but I'm calling bullshit if walking in on your wife cheating on you takes you from 7 to 4. <br /> <br /> And &quot;How did the Beast's brother get to integrity 4&quot; was more a &quot;this is the kind of thing that is obviously going to result in changes in personality. Why the fuck dind't the Beast or someone else not notice these changes before their brother went from 7 to 4?&quot; Not a &quot;what exactly resulted in them hitting integ 4.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T22:28:46-07:00","id":544818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544762#post544762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<b>No More Heroes:</b> The Beast\u2019s Soul does not cause Heroes to arise. Heroes might still seek the Beast out, but they cannot place Anathema on her and the Hero\u2019s gift of Heroic Tracking is of no use. <b>The Beast Incarnate can remove the Hero\u2019s abilities, granting him clarity and showing him exactly who he is in the scheme of things \u2014 an interloper, an intruder in a story that was never his.</b> With a simple touch, the Beast shows the Hero that no matter how unpleasant the occurrence that turned him into a Hero, no matter how terrifying the nightmare, it\u2019s not his place to end it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Must not have read that bit as carefully as I should have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the person is starting at 7(the average given integrity) it's going to take more than one breaking point to reach integrity four. I'll let someone more statistically minded calculate the exact details, but I'm calling bullshit if walking in on your wife cheating on you takes you from 7 to 4.<br /> <br /> And &quot;How did the Beast's brother get to integrity 4&quot; was more a &quot;this is the kind of thing that is obviously going to result in changes in personality. Why the fuck dind't the Beast or someone else not notice these changes before their brother went from 7 to 4?&quot; Not a &quot;what exactly resulted in them hitting integ 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that the trip to 4 was short or that the Beast didn't notice. They could very well have noticed; I'd most certainly make sure to drop hints about it in any game I'll run long before they turn Hero. A downward spiral in a family member's life has been used as a plot hook for ages. Nor was I suggesting that any single breaking point incident take causes a loss of multiple points of Integrity. All of which is irrelevant to the point I was trying to make.<br /> <br /> But as we are approaching the splat from opposite angles. You are quite right that the rules don't say anything about targeting certain people; anyone who is in an altered state of consciousness (including being unconscious) within [Lair] miles is a potential target. I was asserting that it makes sense from an IC perspective that it [the Soul] would target people it was familiar with because they are 'easy to find' prey. OOC I was saying that choosing characters the PCs interact with to 'Inflict Nightmares' on makes that effect visible to them. &quot;...most Beasts are not going to know <i><b>their </b></i>heroes,&quot; isn't conductive to that. [I'm reading their as an ownership; ie. you made them.]<br /> Simply put, I am approaching the mechanics with a narrative bias in mind; &quot;what would be the most interesting but fair way to make a story?&quot;<br /> In my head the answer to the Topic/Thread's question is straightforward; They aren't necessarily jerks but they haven't been 'healthy' people for awhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 06-08-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T23:51:06-07:00","id":544860,"title":"","content":"Wasn't their a beast who caused a whole police station to have nightmares and only one person got turned into a hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T00:40:56-07:00","id":544891,"title":"","content":"Exactly.<br /> <br /> Not everybody becomes a Hero.<br /> <br /> Only people at a certain level of integrity and even then they don't always become heroes-only with a crit success of dramatic failure on the nightmare roll, or if the Beast dramatic failures the roll of one Nightmare.<br /> <br /> As someone in the other Heroes thread put it, by all logic heroes should be rare-there's a maximum distance and the feedings seem to be random.<br /> <br /> So you just have to happen to be in in soul ravaging distance of someone broken, narcissistic, psychopathic, sociopathic, or whatever the word for &quot;everything bad happens to me is somebody's fault, but that somebody is never me, and those other guys are conspiring against me&quot; is(not paranoia, but...) enough to be one step away from becoming a serial killer, and your soul have to randomly ravage them, and it has to either fuck up it's soul ravaging or do it too well. I imagine most Beasts don't make more than one hero in their lives unless they are deliberately starving themselves and/or they live in a really shitty place to live<br /> <br /> Considering the examples given, I'd expect the first category, the people at integ 4- because they're broken broke themselves (preformed too many deeds they couldn't live with or something like that) than someone who was like, brought that low by continuous abuse or bullying. While it is possible that somebody could theoretically hit enough breaking points to hit four from seven based on continuous abuse, the book calls out bullies and abusers as potential Heroes, so the abuser would be more likely to get Heroed than their victim, me thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T02:23:38-07:00","id":544939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544891#post544891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> or if the Beast dramatic failures the roll of one Nightmare.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find this one. What page is it on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T03:26:26-07:00","id":544957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544818#post544818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as we are approaching the splat from opposite angles. You are quite right that the rules don't say anything about targeting certain people; anyone who is in an altered state of consciousness (including being unconscious) within [Lair] miles is a potential target. I was asserting that it makes sense from an IC perspective that it [the Soul] would target people it was familiar with because they are 'easy to find' prey. OOC I was saying that choosing characters the PCs interact with to 'Inflict Nightmares' on makes that effect visible to them. &quot;...most Beasts are not going to know <i><b>their </b></i>heroes,&quot; isn't conductive to that. [I'm reading their as an ownership; ie. you made them.]<br /> Simply put, I am approaching the mechanics with a narrative bias in mind; &quot;what would be the most interesting but fair way to make a story?&quot;<br /> In my head the answer to the Topic/Thread's question is straightforward; They aren't necessarily jerks but they haven't been 'healthy' people for awhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely i'd say a Beast who's Soul is Rampaging Isn't going too Care (The Soul that is) Where it gets it's Fix from and will go too wherever it can too feed, And feed on what it needs. Someone who Feeds on Fear of Death's Soul may Bee-line for the Nearest Hospitial too feast on all the Mourning in a A&amp;E Department, One on Punishment might Feed from a Police Station (Probably everyone that it can) As that is a place that those Emotions will be high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T05:25:30-07:00","id":545057,"title":"","content":"I don't really think it's a matter of morality. Morality implies agency. It implies free will. I wouldn't consider any of the sample Heroes to be evil before they became Heroes. Jerks, maybe, but not near bad enough to deserve being magically coerced into a suicidal course of action. That doesn't matter, though, because they aren't those people anymore once they become Heroes. They're mindless robots acting how they were magically programmed.<br /> <br /> Calling a Hero evil is like calling the victim of a Vampire's Dominate discipline &quot;evil&quot; when the Vampire tells him to go kill a hobo.<br /> <br /> They just can't be considered morally culpable.<br /> <br /> So my answer to the thread's subject is: neither. They are as dickish as the rock a kid chucks through your window. It isn't their fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:22:19-07:00","id":545105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545057#post545057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think it's a matter of morality. Morality implies agency. It implies free will. I wouldn't consider any of the sample Heroes to be evil before they became Heroes. Jerks, maybe, but not near bad enough to deserve being magically coerced into a suicidal course of action. That doesn't matter, though, because they aren't those people anymore once they become Heroes. They're mindless robots acting how they were magically programmed.<br /> <br /> Calling a Hero evil is like calling the victim of a Vampire's Dominate discipline &quot;evil&quot; when the Vampire tells him to go kill a hobo.<br /> <br /> They just can't be considered morally culpable.<br /> <br /> So my answer to the thread's subject is: neither. They are as dickish as the rock a kid chucks through your window. It isn't their fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well how are they robots each of them act differently we have a guy acting like a medieval knight another treating it like its religious duty to kill heroes none them seem to be acting like each othere heck even one hero simply gave up because her beast simply moved out of town and did nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T07:43:59-07:00","id":545162,"title":"","content":"Given this game's reliance on subverting the monomyth, I'm really surprised that the writers didn't emphasize that the difference between a regular person who might have a nuanced reaction to the depredations of the Beasts is whether the mortal in question accepts the &quot;Call to Adventure&quot;, which is step two of the heroic cycle.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is in fact referenced on page 81: &quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Hero of the story is an earthly paragon. He\u2019s the light that holds the dark at bay. He takes up the call to adventure, he learns wisdom and sacrifice, he dies and resurrects.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the book discredits this on the very next page &quot;...</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">the monster that made him a zealot in the first place. &quot;</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 06-08-2015, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:26:10-07:00","id":545275,"title":"","content":"I think that's sort of the point. It's an enforced cycle, despite how much it convinces its prisoners otherwise. It's forced on those suitable to become Heroes, not by design but by accident and inevitability. And it all uwittingly begins with Beasts.<br /> <br /> Though that bit on page 81 doesn't really seem like something you should take to heart. It's describing a very idealized image of heroic potential - one that has definite dissonance with how Heroes tend to actually be. It comes off to me as a purposeful depiction of what people think when you say the word &quot;hero&quot;, and what Heroes themselves might think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:30:30-07:00","id":545335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545105#post545105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well how are they robots each of them act differently we have a guy acting like a medieval knight another treating it like its religious duty to kill heroes none them seem to be acting like each othere heck even one hero simply gave up because her beast simply moved out of town and did nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't call them robots so much as someone who is mentally unbalanced. They're crazy. If they can get treatment, if they get the appropriate meds, they're good, stable people. That's how I see Heroes. Its kind of like an inverted (and extreme) case of PSTD.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:35:25-07:00","id":545338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545335#post545335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wouldn't call them robots so much as someone who is mentally unbalanced. They're crazy. If they can get treatment, if they get the appropriate meds, they're good, stable people. That's how I see Heroes. Its kind of like an inverted (and extreme) case of PSTD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... Err. Why am i Suddenly thinking of Most Heroes being like the Main Character from Spec Ops: The Line.... Severly Damaged and Wanting too be the Hero of his Story..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:52:45-07:00","id":545360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545338#post545338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm.... Err. Why am i Suddenly thinking of Most Heroes being like the Main Character from Spec Ops: The Line.... Severly Damaged and Wanting too be the Hero of his Story..</div> </div> </div> </div>On the surface but when that starts falling apart when you look deeper into it. Walker's Integrity isn't damaged until the white phosphorus attack and merely wants to speak with Konrad. He doesn't go after him like some wild beast but as a soldier who was wondering just what a friend and a CO is doing. He is far more human than how Beast's Heroes are which seem almost cartoony in nature compared to what Spec Ops offers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:33:24-07:00","id":545403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545360#post545360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the surface but when that starts falling apart when you look deeper into it. Walker's Integrity isn't damaged until the white phosphorus attack and merely wants to speak with Konrad. He doesn't go after him like some wild beast but as a soldier who was wondering just what a friend and a CO is doing. He is far more human than how Beast's Heroes are which seem almost cartoony in nature compared to what Spec Ops offers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See I'd Stat Walker as Integrity 5-6 at the Beginning of the Game and about 4 by the End, He's Not &quot;Evil&quot; he just did what he Thought needed to be done, just he Didn't Realise he was going Nuts. Hints are that he'd been having Delayed PTSD Before and though-out the Game. Leading into the Awesome Ending... But then i Don't Know Fully if you could say he's a &quot;Hero&quot; by the End If he Did Suddenly find that there were monster out there Making people into Chunky Snacks.. I can't Imagine he'd actually have any Response but... &quot;Blah KILL&quot; Atleast if he hasn't had any visits too a Shrink by that point....<br /> <br /> For me That would make him a Sympathetic Hero. He Didn't Ask for this, he's gone though Metahorical Hell, and Now he Finds there Really are Monsters out there Making the World Worse.<br /> <br /> I'm Probably making him into Something he's not though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:09:59-07:00","id":545606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545057#post545057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think it's a matter of morality. Morality implies agency. It implies free will. I wouldn't consider any of the sample Heroes to be evil before they became Heroes. Jerks, maybe, but not near bad enough to deserve being magically coerced into a suicidal course of action. That doesn't matter, though, because they aren't those people anymore once they become Heroes. They're mindless robots acting how they were magically programmed.<br /> <br /> Calling a Hero evil is like calling the victim of a Vampire's Dominate discipline &quot;evil&quot; when the Vampire tells him to go kill a hobo.<br /> <br /> They just can't be considered morally culpable.<br /> <br /> So my answer to the thread's subject is: neither. They are as dickish as the rock a kid chucks through your window. It isn't their fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes have to the option to fight their role and be rehabilitated.<br /> <br /> It might not happen often, but it's still an option.<br /> <br /> for it to even be possible, they have to have free will.<br /> <br /> One of the differences between Beasts and Heroes called out in the text is the fact that, while Beasts are capable of fighting the role they're assigned(Being the Designated Villain) and redefining their place in the story, Heroes almost never even try to fight there roll(The Designated Hero) een though that role makes them do morally reprehensible things.<br /> <br /> Not trying to fight an artificially placed Urge makes you culpable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:22:03-07:00","id":545632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545606#post545606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the differences between Beasts and Heroes called out in the text is the fact that, while Beasts are capable of fighting the role they're assigned(Being the Designated Villain) and redefining their place in the story, Heroes almost never even try to fight there roll(The Designated Hero) een though that role makes them do morally reprehensible things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've Previously stated.... Everything in Modern Storytelling places the &quot;Hero&quot; as the chosen one, the one that Wins, the &quot;Good Guy&quot; Why would someone who's just Found out that Monsters are Real (Via a Dream too add to it) EVER Question that they aren't The &quot;Good Guy&quot; and Chosen too Kill this thing.<br /> <br /> If your Looking for the game adding Commentary on something... That's it. We Always Tell story that the &quot;Hero&quot; is always in the Right Regardless of what he Does. Aslong as he Prevails then he Wins and.... History is Written By the Victors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:26:28-07:00","id":545638,"title":"","content":"Heroes remind me of D&amp;D in a way. You can be a murder hobo, going around killing things without a care because they're an &quot;evil race&quot; and still call yourself Good. Nevermind that those evil races have families, economy, mothers that have to raise their kids, very likely have agricultural or hunter/gatherer roots... Its kind of amusing in a way that the evil beings in D&amp;D fall apart when you try to look at them in any depth.<br /> <br /> Its that mentality, I think, that Heroes end up with. They slay the monsters. Why, because they're monsters, no matter who, what, when, where, how, and why the monster actually is. They don't bother looking closely, because why should they? <br /> <br /> And, yes, there's now a high probability of a group of Heroes consisting of Fighter, Black Mage, White Mage, and Thief in my first Beast game now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-08-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:35:06-07:00","id":545643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545638#post545638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, yes, there's now a high probability of a group of Heroes consisting of Fighter, Black Mage, White Mage, and Thief in my first Beast game now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Constantly Snipe at Each other and Actively want too try and Kill Each other? (Except for the Fighter who's too Nice/much of an Idiot too realise they are Trying too Get rid of him?)<br /> Ow and the &quot;Hunter&quot;/Red Mage that is Constantly saying about his Stats? And the Thief Has a Contract that states he Owns whatever they find, even if one of the others owns it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:45:07-07:00","id":545662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545632#post545632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've Previously stated.... Everything in Modern Storytelling places the &quot;Hero&quot; as the chosen one, the one that Wins, the &quot;Good Guy&quot; Why would someone who's just Found out that Monsters are Real (Via a Dream too add to it) EVER Question that they aren't The &quot;Good Guy&quot; and Chosen too Kill this thing.<br /> <br /> If your Looking for the game adding Commentary on something... That's it. We Always Tell story that the &quot;Hero&quot; is always in the Right Regardless of what he Does. Aslong as he Prevails then he Wins and.... History is Written By the Victors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure how this relates to my post, but I'd imagine if you have a compulsion to kill the &quot;monster&quot; and this compulsion leads you to try and blow up an orphanage, not fighting the compulsion makes you fully culpable in blowing up the orphanage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:57:51-07:00","id":545668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545662#post545662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite sure how this relates to my post, but I'd imagine if you have a compulsion to kill the &quot;monster&quot; and this compulsion leads you to try and blow up an orphanage, not fighting the compulsion makes you fully culpable in blowing up the orphanage.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Part i was just trying too give people examples and support your Point.<br /> <br /> Second, Agreed, But they might not understand it because &quot;Heroes can do Horrible things Because they are the Good Guys&quot; Not an Excuse but a reason as too why they need someone else too Stop them and Explain it too them. I see Heroes as Something Akin too Paladin Alexander Alexson from Hellsing. He Kills People who he sees as &quot;Heretics&quot; and Supporting Monsters just because he can and because he feels justified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:06:55-07:00","id":545700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545638#post545638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its that mentality, I think, that Heroes end up with. They slay the monsters. Why, because they're monsters, no matter who, what, when, where, how, and why the monster actually is. They don't bother looking closely, because why should they?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda get the mental image of that Tyrant who works as a health inspector accidentally making a hero out of a restaurateur who just never cleaned his place to save a few bucks and didn't give a fuck about anybody but himself and his wallet(In this case, he's at 4 do to being extremely sociopathic, not from any breaking points he suffered-he started at 4)-The Beast wasn't able to go through his full routine and wasn't able to properly feed on that shut down, and his soul just so happened to towards the owner later that night.<br /> <br /> Eventually the Hero gets picked up by a cell of tier one hunters, and he directs them to his quarry.<br /> <br /> The stakeout:<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you sure this guy is a monster? He's sort of just go about his day. Yeah he's a hard ass, but it is kinda his job.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You don't' understand, he crushes the dreams of inspiring restructures and feeds on their despair. I know, it's happened to me. I wouldn't be surprised if he wasn't somehow using his powers to plant things to find.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;okay...&quot;<br /> <br /> *Later*<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh come on, he's having a tea party with his five year old niece&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh no, it's just a trick to throw suspicion off of himself&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay...&quot;<br /> <br /> *later*<br /> <br /> &quot;He just killed that Slasher we lost track of a weak ago&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Getting rid of the competition&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He saved all of those kids when the orphanage burned down. Noone got hurt.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He probably started the fire himself to make himself look like a hero&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But the fireman said it was an electrical fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;what does he know?&quot;<br /> <br /> *later*<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, it turns out that vampire we were investigating last month murdered five people, including my <i>son</i>, while we were investigating your 'monster.' You're out fo the cell&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You fools! Can't you see that The Health Inspector is more dangerous than any vampire! What's your son worth compared to taking down this mosnter for good?!&quot;<br /> <br /> *Later, on the news&quot;<br /> <br /> A Former Restaurant Owner was found dead of multiple stabwounds in a ditch the other day. Police suspect the (whatever name the media gave the slasher) is the culprit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:13:44-07:00","id":545708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545668#post545668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, Agreed, But they might not understand it because &quot;Heroes can do Horrible things Because they are the Good Guys&quot; Not an Excuse but a reason as too why they need someone else too Stop them and Explain it too them. I see Heroes as Something Akin too Paladin Alexander Alexson from Hellsing. He Kills People who he sees as &quot;Heretics&quot; and Supporting Monsters just because he can and because he feels justified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not people he &quot;sees&quot; as heretics. He explicitly hates protestants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:52:48-07:00","id":545907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545708#post545708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not people he &quot;sees&quot; as heretics. He explicitly hates protestants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alexander Anderson is an amazing example of a Hero... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> He does however later help Hellsing multiple times, including being an escort for Integra Hellsing through the Millennium infested London when left on her own, not outright killing her. He also goes ahead and later kills Enrico Maxwell, his own superior when Maxwell goes drunk with power and has his Crusaders start killing random innocents on the excuse he is waging war on Protestants. Then we get to the massive duel he has with Alucard, clearly his Beast analogy here. Notable that Alucard was playing with kid-gloves and hoped Anderson would beat him, because he was a man pure of faith with strong morals/ethics (you decide) and as strong as Van Helsing and deserved to beat the monster.<br /> But Anderson decided when chips were down to become a monster himself and so Alucard takes off the kid-gloves. Whilst Anderson very much does sit in a narrative standpoint of being a Hero in that he was pretty much (outside of Walter) the main rival of the Protagonist Beast and was a side-character in the Beast's story... I don't think Anderson showed too low an Integrity until Alucard handed his ass to him enough that he pulled the Nail out to become a monster himself. I'd call him more a straight Hunter than a Hero, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:57:56-07:00","id":545919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545907#post545907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alexander Anderson is an amazing example of a Hero... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> He does however later help Hellsing multiple times, including being an escort for Integra Hellsing through the Millennium infested London when left on her own, not outright killing her. He also goes ahead and later kills Enrico Maxwell, his own superior when Maxwell goes drunk with power and has his Crusaders start killing random innocents on the excuse he is waging war on Protestants. Then we get to the massive duel he has with Alucard, clearly his Beast analogy here. Notable that Alucard was playing with kid-gloves and hoped Anderson would beat him, because he was a man pure of faith with strong morals/ethics (you decide) and as strong as Van Helsing and deserved to beat the monster.<br /> But Anderson decided when chips were down to become a monster himself and so Alucard takes off the kid-gloves. Whilst Anderson very much does sit in a narrative standpoint of being a Hero in that he was pretty much (outside of Walter) the main rival of the Protagonist Beast and was a side-character in the Beast's story... I don't think Anderson showed too low an Integrity until Alucard handed his ass to him enough that he pulled the Nail out to become a monster himself. I'd call him more a straight Hunter than a Hero, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I consider Aderson to be the hunter the real hero I considered was the Major who dedicated his whole life to killing Alucard and destroying all of England just get to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:22:54-07:00","id":545958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545919#post545919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I consider Aderson to be the hunter the real hero I considered was the Major who dedicated his whole life to killing Alucard and destroying all of England just get to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anderson is a Hero Prior too the Ireland Fight and Maybe abit After it, Post that he's a Hunter (Borderline Slasher, Integrity 5). Then he Uses an Artifact and Goes full on Beast...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:23:29-07:00","id":545959,"title":"","content":"I'd also say perhaps Walter could class as a Hero too, that man held his grudge on Alucard for 55 years (highly hinted to stem from Alucard leaving Walter to handle the Captain alone in 1944 on their Mission, where Captain then curb-stomped the young lad) and had to have had his Integrity knocked to be in the position to place himself to the position where he could fight and beat Alucard. I'd have said in that regards then that the Beast that awoke Walter to being the Hero was the Captain, through their two encounters split 55 years apart and it just so happens he blames Alucard and decides to target him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T17:47:24-07:00","id":546165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=545708#post545708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not people he &quot;sees&quot; as heretics. He explicitly hates protestants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, I believe one of his earlier quotes is calling Integra a &quot;Filthy, protestant whore.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rather funny since he gets off a train, sees a real whore and says &quot;go with god, child.&quot; as he smiles.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't call the Major a hero by any stretch of the word. Yes, he did want to kill Alucard, but at the same time he wanted a massive, endless war. He didn't care about wealth or power or even his own troops, he just wanted violence and destruction.<br /> <br /> I don't think Hellsing had any Hero allegories except possibly Integra herself. Her mission is to wipe out monsters, and instead her family spent 100 years enhancing a monster's already supernatural abilities in order to turn him into a weapon against his own kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7OsJA7Vc53w\" data-code=\"7OsJA7Vc53w\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7OsJA7Vc53w/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-08-2015, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:03:04-07:00","id":546205,"title":"","content":"The Major was a Beast.<br /> <br /> If he was not, best of all, an extremely dangerous mortal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And <i>yes</i>, Anderson was a hero. In my opinion, he was both the best and the worst of Heroes. A bloodthirsty psychopath convinced of his own divine worth as a sanctified yet damned tool of God. At the same time, remarkably human and understanding, motivated by the lost youth and perpetually keeping them in mind, and offering aid to Integra, Seras, and even extending a final comfort to <i>Alucard of all people</i> as he was dying. Anderson was everything glorious and damnable about the Heroic Paradigm, admirable and detestable all at once. If you can make a Hero like him in your game, <i>you've succeeded</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't recall him calling Integra a whore, oddly enough. I think that was all Maxwell, though it's been a while since I've read Hellsing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-08-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:38:15-07:00","id":546274,"title":"","content":"Maxwell called Integra a Protestant <i>Sow, </i>not whore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:45:03-07:00","id":546276,"title":"","content":"Eh. As I say, it's been a while since I've read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:47:10-07:00","id":546282,"title":"","content":"A lot of people mention Ahab as a good example of the Heroes, and I agree. He is not &quot;evil&quot; per se, but he clearly is losing it, leading him to be a huge dick (pun may or may not be intended) who not only maniacally pursue his beast, but also causes a whole lot of collateral damage.<br /> <br /> In that sense, I am not to keen on the writers calling the heroes with terms like &quot;jerks,&quot; because such terms does not do justice; heroes, while being delusional, should not just be dismissed as being one-dimensional and irredeemable. The tragedy should come from actually being able to be easily redeemed, but not choosing that path for own ego.<br /> <br /> While I admire him, I can't forgive Matt for making Gaston analogy. That kind of ruined all Heroes for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:53:47-07:00","id":546291,"title":"","content":"Would it help if he had called them Avenant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T18:55:40-07:00","id":546294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=546282#post546282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people mention Ahab as a good example of the Heroes, and I agree. He is not &quot;evil&quot; per se, but he clearly is losing it, leading him to be a huge dick (pun may or may not be intended) who not only maniacally pursue his beast, but also causes a whole lot of collateral damage.<br /> <br /> In that sense, I am not to keen on the writers calling the heroes with terms like &quot;jerks,&quot; because such terms does not do justice; heroes, while being delusional, should not just be dismissed as being one-dimensional and irredeemable. The tragedy should come from actually being able to be easily redeemed, but not choosing that path for own ego.<br /> <br /> While I admire him, I can't forgive Matt for making Gaston analogy. That kind of ruined all Heroes for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well which analogy would you prefer I would have jack the beanstalk from discworld.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\">Jack chopped down what was the world\u2019s last beanstalk, adding murder and ecological terrorism to the theft, enticement and trespass charges already mentioned, and all the giant\u2019s children didn\u2019t have a daddy any more. But he got away with it and lived happily ever after without so much as a guilty twinge about what he had done. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:59:46-07:00","id":546606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=546205#post546205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't recall him calling Integra a whore, oddly enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>He calls her &quot;Babylon&quot;, i.e. the Whore of Babylon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:35:39-07:00","id":546628,"title":"","content":"He is however very gentlemanly towards her when London is burning down and she is left without Walter... At the part where he is leading a whole bunch of Iscariot Priests with Heinkel and Yumi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T11:30:49-07:00","id":549079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=544762#post544762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<b>No More Heroes:</b> The Beast\u2019s Soul does not cause Heroes to arise. Heroes might still seek the Beast out, but they cannot place Anathema on her and the Hero\u2019s gift of Heroic Tracking is of no use. <b>The Beast Incarnate can remove the Hero\u2019s abilities, granting him clarity and showing him exactly who he is in the scheme of things \u2014 an interloper, an intruder in a story that was never his.</b> With a simple touch, the Beast shows the Hero that no matter how unpleasant the occurrence that turned him into a Hero, no matter how terrifying the nightmare, it\u2019s not his place to end it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously not everyone will agree with me on this, but I read that passage to be a bit like Morpheus' actions in the Sandman comic at the end of the 'Cereal Convention'. He strips away the dreams and fantasies of the serial killers where they are justified or the hero or persecuted and misunderstood, leaving them only the stark truth of their petty monstrosity.<br /> <br /> The Incarnate Beast doesn't make the Hero a mortal again, only shatters their power and delusion to reveal the misguided loser underneath. It leaves them a broken puppet still saddled with the need to kill, now mostly smothered under despair. Not the Hero of the story, only a footnote in the legend of something greater and grander than himself.<br /> <br /> Being able to rescue a Hero and send them back to a normal life feels too clean cut, and far too kind, for the ascended living legend of a primordial nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:51:20-07:00","id":549318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=549079#post549079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously not everyone will agree with me on this, but I read that passage to be a bit like Morpheus' actions in the Sandman comic at the end of the 'Cereal Convention'. He strips away the dreams and fantasies of the serial killers where they are justified or the hero or persecuted and misunderstood, leaving them only the stark truth of their petty monstrosity.<br /> <br /> The Incarnate Beast doesn't make the Hero a mortal again, only shatters their power and delusion to reveal the misguided loser underneath. It leaves them a broken puppet still saddled with the need to kill, now mostly smothered under despair. Not the Hero of the story, only a footnote in the legend of something greater and grander than himself.<br /> <br /> Being able to rescue a Hero and send them back to a normal life feels too clean cut, and far too kind, for the ascended living legend of a primordial nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Agree and Disagree, I Believe all it'll do is show them Clarity, That they are Nuts and Not a &quot;Hero&quot; just someone Compelled too hunt and &quot;Feed&quot; on Monsters... Just Like the Monsters they Hunt are Compelled too feed. Show them the Mirror and the Clarity that they Need to Stop them being Heroes... Now they have NOTHING. Broken shell of a Man or Women is all that'll be left, Whether they recover is up too what they do with them after.<br /> <br /> Basically they CAN have a &quot;happy&quot; ending, but they'll need too earn it After they've been shown the Truth of just how Wretched they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T03:24:21-07:00","id":549937,"title":"","content":"From what I've read so far it seems like Heroes are ordinary people (for the World of Darkness anyway) who were already on the edge thanks to their own shortcomings or unfortunate circumstances, who were just given the opportunity to go full long into the plunge. In that regard they are the ultimate embodyment of Transferance (think that's the right term anyways), flawed people who could use a sholder to lean on who glimps true supernatural horror and splendor in the form of the Beast's Soul and turn that into a symbol for all of their grief, hate, fear, and desire. This trapps them in a cycle of violence that will eventually erode away the last bits of Integrity they have untless they are slain or begin to climb out of the pit they've thrown themselves into, and all because they refused to see that they made the Beasts the target of their obsession. For a Hero isn't magically controlled or influenced by the Beast, they simple get a taste of it's power but see it as a Call to Action instead of what it really is: an escape from their own life.<br /> <br /> I feel the best example of this comes from the primary difference between Hunters and Heroes. Hunters take on the Vigil primarily because the discovery of the Supernatural and realize that their lives will never be the same again after such a revelation and choose to either make the most of the situation they find themselves in (and become stupid-rich in the process) or because they truly wish to protect others from the same horros of the world that forever changed their lives. On the other hand a Hero activly takes on the mantel as either a way to make their lives better (either through returning things to an hypothetical bettter time or by destroying the imagined cause of all of their grief) or to give meaning to a life they believed to be empty and meaningless. There will of course be some overlap in certain circumstances because both are unquestionably human, but generally a Hero is a Hero because they now refuse to be anything less. Because to do so would be to go back to what they were before that fatefull nightmare, just a scared human being.<br /> <br /> (Side Note: Is it really true that Hunter have to have Integrety 4 to become Slashers? Because oh my god the implications! Beasts can gain Kinship with Slashers, and the Lucifuge which is hillarious and a tip of the hat to Hunter the Vigil, so what could this mean? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:36:57-07:00","id":550100,"title":"","content":"Morality of 4 or below. Morality was more specifically how bad you were. Integrity is your mental well being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:39:33-07:00","id":550104,"title":"","content":"In a way, Beast: the Primordial and Hunter: the Vigil are opposites.<br /> <br /> In HtV, you play a human that hunts the monsters that creep in the dark to protect humanity from their evil and terror. The game reduces the other supernaturals to a point where all are treated as a large extended family of monsters (usually via the Inferno, the collective sins of humanity).<br /> <br /> In BtP, you play the monster that creeps in the dark and inflicts terror on humanity, and are hunted by a human that wants to slay evil. The game pulls in all other supernaturals to the point where everyone is the same family through the collective fears and dark urges of humanity.<br /> <br /> The two games are hitting similar themes on different sides. So, in a way, Heroes really are just a variant hunter template, but with a very specific tie to Beast, and super-emphasizes all the different mental issues that comes with being a hunter. Its unsurprising that the Heroes and Hunters would be mirror reflections of each other as well. Both are profoundly changed by their exposure to the supernatural. One difference, of course, is that a hero is, by definition, kind of insane. Heroes can't tell the difference between reality and their own illusions. They can't see the harm they're causing.<br /> <br /> That said, there is another side to the whole hero-beast aspects that we haven't looked at, or talked about, in any detail. People look at heroes as &quot;jerks,&quot; &quot;dicks,&quot; or &quot;zealots.&quot; Ironically, the description is actually more appropriate for the Beasts themselves, who are basically the embodiment of all of humanity's sadistic tendencies. Heroes aren't necessarily jerks - in fact, I'd say they generally aren't. They're primarily Knight Templars. They're the fundamentalists that think they're good, but can't see shades of grey. They're the Moral Guardians.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that, where Beasts are the dark aspects of humanity, the dark buried swarms of the id buried below the subconcious level, the Heroes are the super ego that is the seat of all that is &quot;light,&quot; the moral imperatives. And the funny thing about the freudian super ego is that it <i>loves</i> judging others. The thing to remember about Freudian ego, super ego, and id is that good isn't light, but rather, good is the Ego balancing the light and dark in a way that allows empathy and compassion. The two extremes of Hero and Beast are both dangerous. Its also notable that Freud considered the Super Ego to be a completely artificial construct who's purpose was to just restrict the Id. Ironically, that's the same role that Heroes have.<br /> <br /> Heroes are the super ego, the Soul is the id, and the actual human part of the Beast is the Ego that mediates between the morality and the primal drives. And, yes, the Astral does contain all of that as well. Those of you familiar with the Astral in Mage should be familiar with the idea that there's the single daimon that controls and orders the mind, while there are a multitude of goetic demons running around. The daimon is the super ego, the goetic demons are the id. And the conscious mind mediates between these two urges. The strife between a &quot;shoulder angel&quot; and &quot;shoulder devil&quot; is real in the WoD, and that's played out in the battle between Hero and Beast, the embodiments of the human parts of the Astral and human psyche.<br /> <br /> From this perspective, the Heroes being the super ego, a lot of their description makes actual sense. What they do, how they do it. Heroes are as much &quot;non-humans&quot; as the Beast is. They're tapping into a Super Ego Dream, for lack of a better term. The unfortunate thing about the super ego, though, is that its actually not powerful. All the drive, ambition, arousal, energy, and power that humans have come from the id. All the super ego can do is punish through feelings of remorse and guilt. So, from a Fruedian standpoint as much as a mythological one, giving Heroes power equal to the Beasts they &quot;punish&quot; doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> The problem, I think, is that people are used to thinking of the &quot;shoulder angel&quot; as good, and being equal in strength to the &quot;shoulder devil.&quot; I also think that people want to see the Heroes as a kind of major power on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/544317-beast-heroes-necessarily-huge-dicks-or-just-probably?p=549937#post549937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Side Note: Is it really true that Hunter have to have Integrety 4 to become Slashers? Because oh my god the implications! Beasts can gain Kinship with Slashers, and the Lucifuge which is hillarious and a tip of the hat to Hunter the Vigil, so what could this mean? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, its true that you need at least <i>Morality </i>4 (remember, 1e rules) in order to become a Slasher. What could this mean?<br /> <br /> Not sure. Low Integrity doesn't really reflect what it means to be a Slasher anymore. Slashers and the Inferno are strongly tied to the idea of objective evil forces in the world. I'm not really sure that Integrity is appropriate to reflect what either of those represent. Low Integrity means you're mentally unstable, and Heroes and Beasts are definitely unbalanced, especially since we're talking about them as inflated super egos and ids. <br /> <br /> Slashers do tend to be insane or broken people, so they're likely low Integrity, but their powers aren't linked to the psyche like a Hero's is. Heroes stop being heroes when their id, ego, and super ego go back into balance (represented by raising Integrity). I don't think that applies to Slashers - they're more of a supernatural monster with an alternative Integrity system that's not really detailed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-11-2015, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}